==============================================================================
klein-S335: the half fold (sigma) and quarter fold (sigma,phi) vs the star split
==============================================================================

--- n=3  m=1 ---
 (A) sigma = rho-induced tile perm, sigma(star v)=star(n+1-v): True;  cut(H) sigma-stable: True
 (B) phi=all-ones in cut(H): True   H bipartite: True   [must agree]
 (C) eps != 0: False   translation law hol(t+1)=hol(t)+eps: True   phi free on orbits: False
 (D) leg(y=1)=1 tiles = star_H(1); leg(x=n)=1 tiles = star_H(n); sigma swaps legs: True
     Fix(sigma) = [(3, 1)]  (antidiagonal x+y=n+1: True, a matching: True)
 (E) dim cut=1 (=n-1: False)  dim cycle=0 (=m-n+1: False)
     star orbits = 2^0;  QUARTER-invariant dim = 0 = m-(n-1)-1
     maxcut(H)=1, defect of phi from cut(H) = m-maxcut = 0

